description: MovieBox-Tui agent guide — architecture, commands and invariants
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before making changes. It is the source of truth for
the architecture, the verified build/test commands and the invariants that must not be
broken.

Quick rules:
- Rust 1.90+, edition 2024. `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --all-targets
  --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace`.
- Core code (`src/cache.rs`, `src/service.rs`, `src/providers/`, `src/util.rs`, …) must
  not depend on `src/tui/`. The Android app links the crate with
  `default-features = false` (the terminal UI is behind the `tui` feature).
- The terminal UI is message-driven: add an `Action` variant and a `handle_*` method in
  `src/tui/app/`; never block the event loop; mutate `AppState` only inside
  `handle_action`.
- Replay `User-Agent`, `Referer` and the CloudFront cookie on every stream request.
- No panics on network or user-input paths. Zero telemetry. Conventional Commits.
- Four `player::tests::*` / playback tests fail on machines with `mpv`/`vlc` installed;
  that is pre-existing, do not weaken those assertions.
